@page "/demo/barcodes"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared

@* 2026-10-12: new page on FeatureDemoLayout; two examples (barcode, QR code). Facts checked against BarcodeControl.razor, QrCodeControl.razor,
   BarcodeModels.cs, their stylesheets and FlexCore.csproj (ZXing.Net 0.16.11) in FlexCore 0.2.48. Both moved here from UI elements. *@

<PageTitle>Barcodes & QR — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Barcodes & QR" Category="Components" ControlName="BarcodeControl · QrCodeControl"
                   Tagline="Nine linear symbologies and QR codes, encoded on the server and drawn as inline SVG."
                   SourcePath="BarcodeControl.razor; QrCodeControl.razor; BarcodeModels.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            Both controls hand <code>Value</code> to ZXing.Net and render the result as an <code>&lt;svg role="img"&gt;</code>, so there is
            no image request and the code scales with its box. A value the symbology cannot encode shows the encoder's message in place of the
            code instead of throwing. <code>BarcodeControl</code> picks the symbology with <code>Type</code>; <code>QrCodeControl</code> takes a
            <code>Size</code> and an <code>ErrorCorrection</code> level.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="barcode" Title="Barcode" RazorCode="@Code.Barcode" CSharpCode="@Code.BarcodeCs">
            <Description><p>Pick a symbology and edit the value. Each one has its own rules: EAN-13 wants 12 or 13 digits, UPC-A 11 or 12, ITF an even count, Code 39 upper-case letters and digits. Break a rule and the control's own error replaces the bars.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="controls">
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_typeItems" Values="@(new[] { _type.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="PickType" AriaLabel="Symbology" />
                    <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_barcodeValue" UpdateOnInput="true" Width="200px" Placeholder="Value to encode" />
                    <ToggleButtonControl @bind-Selected="_showText">Show text</ToggleButtonControl>
                </div>
                <BarcodeControl Value="@(_barcodeValue ?? "")" Type="_type" ShowText="_showText" BarHeight="60" />
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="qr" Title="QR code" RazorCode="@Code.Qr" CSharpCode="@Code.QrCs">
            <Description><p>Higher error correction survives more damage to the printed code but needs more modules for the same text. <code>Size</code> is the rendered width and height in pixels; the module grid stays sharp because the SVG uses <code>shape-rendering="crispEdges"</code>.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="controls">
                    <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_qrValue" UpdateOnInput="true" Width="280px" Placeholder="Text or URL" />
                    <ButtonGroupControl Items="_eccItems" Values="@(new[] { _ecc.ToString() })" ValuesChanged="PickEcc" AriaLabel="Error correction" />
                </div>
                <div class="qr-row">
                    <QrCodeControl Value="@(_qrValue ?? "")" Size="@Size" ErrorCorrection="_ecc" />
                    <div class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Size @Size px</span>
                        <SliderControl @bind-Value="_size" Min="80" Max="240" Step="20" ShowValue="false" aria-label="QR code size" />
                    </div>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-barcodecontrol-parameters" Title="BarcodeControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Barcode.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="BarcodeControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Barcode" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-barcodetype" Title="BarcodeType" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Types.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="BarcodeType" Rows="Vocab.Types" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-qrcodecontrol-parameters" Title="QrCodeControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Qr.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="QrCodeControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Qr" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-qrerrorcorrectionlevel" Title="QrErrorCorrectionLevel" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Ecc.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="QrErrorCorrectionLevel" Rows="Vocab.Ecc" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-read-only-properties" Title="Read-only properties" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Props.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="Read-only properties" Rows="Vocab.Props" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-css-classes" Title="CSS classes" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Css.Length, "classes")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.CssClasses" Title="CSS classes" Rows="Vocab.Css" />
                <p>Neither stylesheet reads a <code>--fx-*</code> variable. Colours of the code itself come from <code>ForegroundColor</code> and <code>BackgroundColor</code>; the frame is fixed in CSS.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ul>
            <li>The SVG is <code>role="img"</code> with an <code>aria-label</code> that defaults to "<em>Type</em> barcode: <em>value</em>" or "QR code: <em>value</em>". Set <code>AriaLabel</code> when the value is not meaningful to read out.</li>
            <li>An encoding error renders as <code>role="alert"</code> text inside the frame.</li>
            <li>Nothing here is focusable or interactive; the controls above the codes are ordinary FlexCore inputs.</li>
            <li>The barcode's human-readable text is drawn inside the SVG at 11px monospace; it is not selectable. Print the value next to the code if users must copy it.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Badges, cards and the other small display controls: <a href="demo/new-components">UI elements</a>.</li>
            <li>Codes inside printed output: <a href="demo/reports/model-costs">Report writer</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

